From 63b5446be87ed62d1198dcfb08a0020d1b82e0b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:14:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: restart once after LOS without an SFP

When the fibre is pulled in O5, TO2 finds the optical link still down,
stops the MAC and powers the PHY off, and relies on gpon_sfp_link_up()
to restart the session once the light is back. A board with an optical
frontend instead of an SFP (Archer XR500v) never gets that callback,
and with the PHY off nothing polls the link any more: the ONU stays in
O1 until reboot.

Without an SFP bus, schedule one restart after the orderly stop. The
MAC then waits in O2 with the PHY powered, and the session resumes when
the fibre returns. It is a single restart, not a periodic loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index eb691391c..4208e3c7b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -2677,6 +2677,18 @@ static void gpon_to2_work_fn(struct work_struct *work)
 		dev_warn(priv->dev,
 			 "GPON TO2 expired in O6 with the optical link still down, waiting for the fibre\n");
 		gpon_disable(priv);
+		/*
+		 * With an SFP, gpon_sfp_link_up() restarts the session when
+		 * the fibre is back.  An optical frontend has no such
+		 * notification, and gpon_disable() powered the PHY off, so
+		 * nothing would ever notice the light returning.  Restart once:
+		 * the MAC then waits in O2 with the PHY powered and resumes
+		 * when the fibre comes back.
+		 */
+		if (!priv->sfp_bus && READ_ONCE(priv->started) &&
+		    READ_ONCE(priv->optical_active))
+			mod_delayed_work(priv->fsm_wq, &priv->restart_work,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(GPON_DEACTIVATE_RESTART_MS));
 		return;
 	}
 
